# Snowflake SPCS Native App Development

## When to Apply

Apply when user mentions: "native app" + "Snowflake", "SPCS", "Snowpark Container Services", "MCP server" + "Snowflake", or hosting services in Snowflake.

## Reference

- **Project**: `/Users/mxu/native-apps-examples/mcp-server-app-v1/`
- **Full Guide**: `SPCS_NATIVE_APP_DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md`

## Project Structure

```
my-app/
├── app/
│   ├── manifest.yml          # Privileges, endpoints, callbacks
│   ├── setup.sql             # Roles, procedures, MCP SERVER
│   └── README.md
├── backend/
│   ├── Dockerfile
│   └── src/app.py
├── prepare/
│   ├── provider_setup.sql
│   └── consumer_setup.sql
├── snowflake.yml             # CLI project definition
├── backend.yaml.template
├── setup.sh
└── deploy.sh
```

## Essential Patterns

### snowflake.yml
```yaml
definition_version: 1
native_app:
  name: <app_name>
  source_stage: napp.app_stage
  artifacts:
    - src: app/*
      dest: ./
  package:
    name: <app_name>_pkg
    role: naspcs_role
    warehouse: wh_nap
  application:
    name: <app_name>_instance
    role: nac
    warehouse: wh_nac
```

### Manifest V2 (Auto-Granted Privileges)
```yaml
manifest_version: 2
version:
  name: V1
  label: "First Version"

artifacts:
  setup_script: setup.sql
  readme: README.md

privileges:
  - CREATE COMPUTE POOL:
      description: "Create compute pools"
  - BIND SERVICE ENDPOINT:
      description: "Public ingress"
```

### Service Function (SQL → HTTP)
```sql
CREATE FUNCTION v1.my_tool(input VARCHAR)
RETURNS VARCHAR
SERVICE = app_public.backend
ENDPOINT = api
AS '/my_endpoint';
```

### Backend Handler (for service functions)
```python
@app.route("/my_endpoint", methods=['POST'])
def handler():
    data = request.get_json()
    if 'data' in data:  # Service function format
        results = [[row[0], f"Result: {row[1]}"] for row in data['data']]
        return jsonify(data=results)
```

### MCP SERVER
```sql
CREATE MCP SERVER v1.my_mcp_server
FROM SPECIFICATION $$
tools:
- title: "My Tool"
  identifier: "<app_instance>.v1.my_tool"
  name: "my_tool"
  type: "GENERIC"
  description: "Tool description"
  config:
    type: "function"
    warehouse: "WH_NAC"
    input_schema:
      type: "object"
      properties:
        input:
          type: "string"
$$;
```

## Deployment

```bash
export SNOWFLAKE_DEFAULT_CONNECTION_NAME=<connection>
./setup.sh    # Creates resources, builds/pushes Docker
./deploy.sh   # Runs: snow app run
# Then in Snowsight: Grant → Activate → Launch App
```

## MCP REST API Auth

```bash
curl -X POST "https://<account>.snowflakecomputing.com/api/v2/databases/<app>/schemas/v1/mcp-servers/<server>" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <PAT>" \
  -H "X-Snowflake-Authorization-Token-Type: PROGRAMMATIC_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/list"}'
```
